WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:15.348
Our production designer and his team
have done such a fantastic job of

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.435
not only creating cool environments,
but sticking to this idea

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:21.855
that I think is so central
to the show of functionality.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.941
When I met Matt and Ben, I felt like
we had a connection right away.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:28.236
I was attracted to this show
for all of the possibilities

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:31.072
of where we had been
and where we were going to go.

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.616
In the writers room,
we’re throwing things out and we're like, 

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:35.994
“Well, what if there's the surface
level of the base?

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:37.579
But then there's an underground level,

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:39.998
and what if there's 
an asteroid hunting ship?

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:43.334
But then there's also 
other types of ships and rovers?” 

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:47.338
and Seth was able to give us like 95%
of what we came up with,

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:49.716
which is insane.

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:51.801
Let’s just hope this doesn't get to his head.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.345
I'm surprised it still fits in his helmet.

00:00:56.014 --> 00:01:00.560
Both on the moon and even on Mars,
shapes will not be square.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.687
They'll be round or oval

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:06.566
because of the difference between
inside pressure and outside pressure.

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:08.777
One of the big things
we keep coming up against

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:10.904
is that building a lot of structures
on the surface

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.947
makes no sense
because of the radiation risk.

00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:14.115
That was a really exciting idea.

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:16.076
Like, what does that mean
to go underground

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:19.412
and how do you make
the world underground feel different?

00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:22.999
We used references from naval vessels.

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:24.375
You walk down a hallway,

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.961
and you feel like you're at the bottom
of a battleship.

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:31.174
Astronauts and cosmonauts, scientists
and pilots, they all work together.

00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:33.301
But us down here,
at the end of the day,

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:35.637
we are just the help.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.973
The barrel-vaulted spaces
like the commissary or

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:42.811
the greenhouse are an incredible
look because it's translucent.

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:46.481
You can see that
there's orange light coming in.

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:48.775
The most beautiful thing

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:52.904
I have ever seen.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:54.072
In the United States,

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:57.867
of course, we ended Season 3
with everything getting blown up.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.496
Mission Control was destroyed
to the point that it needed

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:05.291
to be rebuilt
within the same existing shell.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.418
So now it has a whole new look.

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:10.421
It's got new consoles, new lighting.

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:12.215
Everything's been redone.

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:14.843
The colors, the finishes.

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:17.971
Today, we embrace the 21st century,

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:21.141
the beginning of a new era.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.644
We have a whole side of our story
that's in the Soviet Union.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:28.857
I was fortunate to be part of a scout
to two countries,

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:33.194
 Bulgaria and to Lithuania, where we were able
to gather a lot of research.

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:36.948
It highlighted for me
the differences stylistically

00:02:36.948 --> 00:02:39.367
that's so different between here and there.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:44.289
The work we will do together
will take us far into the cosmos.

00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:48.042
I could never have done this project
without the support that I've had.

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:52.046
The cinematographers,
the visual effects people, everybody.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.257
It's an incredible collaboration.

00:02:56.217 --> 00:03:00.638
None of it would have been possible
without all of you.

